        {
          "id": "SP_ISODICTYA_KERGUELENENSIS",
          "name": "Isodictya kerguelenensis",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Isodictya",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Figure 5 g – i) Restricted synonymy: Homoeodictya kerguelenensis Ridley & Dendy, 1886, Isodictya antarctica (Kirkpatrick, 1908), Isodictya cactoides (Kirkpatrick, 1908). Material examined: 3 specimens collected in stations 10 (SOI; 60 ° 59 ' S, 46 ° 43 ' W; 307 m; 5 / 3 / 2014; MACN-In 44379; IEO-CSIC Col.) and 18 (SOI; 60 ° 47,561 ' S, 45 ° 36,854 ' W; 96 m; 10 / 3 / 2012; MACN-In 44380). Description: Polymorphic species, with a massive or erect and digitiform morphology. Specimens are not flexible. Grey-light, beige in colour (Figure 5 g). The largest specimen here studied had rizhoids at its base. The choanosomal skeleton is made of multispicular tracts of oxeas. The ectosomal skeleton is very fragile, not always present, depending on the preservation state of the specimen. Spicules are thick straight or slightly curved oxeas 530 – 750 µm × 20 – 30 µm, although some thinner oxeas (probably in-formation spicules) were also present (about 10 – 15 µm). Small palmate isochelae of 15 – 25 µm are present but not very common in our specimens (Figure 5 h – i). Remarks: This species has been recorded from Antarctic waters (many times with its synonyms) by Topsent (1908), Burton (1938), Boury-Esnault & Van Beveren (1982), Ríos et al. (2004), and Göcke & Janussen (2013), among others. Our specimens agree with the descriptions in Ríos et al. (2004) and Göcke & Janussen (2013). This is a new record for the SOI.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2244344",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "758cddd0-fc4f-547-a57-59663845c412ad"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_ISODICTYA_LANKESTERI",
          "name": "Isodictya lankesteri",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Isodictya",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Figure 5 m – p) Restricted synonymy: Cercidochela lankesteri Kirkpatrick, 1907. Material examined: 2 specimens collected at station 16 (SOI; 60 ° 40,992 ' S, 46 ° 14,560 ' W; 104 m; 7 / 3 / 2012; MACN-In 44378; IEO-CSIC Col.). Description: One large arborescent specimen, 43 cm high, and a small broken cylindrical specimen, light beige in colour. The larger and complete specimen has a velvety surface, with multiple oscula evident on the branches, the oscula are roughly aligned. The rhizoid anchor structure is conspicuous and has sediment grains and small pebbles attached (Fig. 5 m). The skeleton is composed of ascending plumose multispicular tracts of oxeas. These are connected by other oxeas (Figure 5 p). Microscleres are abundant and dispersed throughout the choanosome. Megascleres are oxeas 270 – 430 µm by 10 – 20 µm; microscleres are canonochelae of 50 – 70 µm (Figure 5 n, o). Remarks: This species was previously recorded by Hentschel (1914), Burton (1929), Desqueyroux (1975), Campos et al. (2007) and Fernández et al. (2021), amongst others. This is a new record for the SOI.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:2244410",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "df2fb621-0694-551-b3d-78a3d28f1993b3"
        },
